<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed weaker at -1.07 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed weaker at -1.07 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland said on Thursday it fixed the zloty at 3.4870 to the dollar, down from 3.4850 on Wednesday, and at 1.9000 to the mark, also down from 1.8905.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.07 percent weaker than the weighted dollar and mark parity rates versus Wednesday's fixing at -0.89 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
